  "summary": "One busy machine and two Runs queued behind it, both reading the same hundred gigabyte corpus. The machine is asked for it once and starts reading. Both callers withdraw at the same moment. The first withdrawal changes nothing about what the machine should be doing, because the second Run still wants the corpus, and Mercator restarts on it. The second withdrawal is the one the restarted control plane reads. What the restarted control plane wants now is nothing, and nothing is also what a control plane that has never asked for anything wants. Those two are the same set and not the same fact: one is a machine reading a hundred gigabytes for Runs that no longer exist, and the other is a fleet with nothing in flight. A control plane that cannot tell them apart stays quiet, the transfer runs to completion, and the room comes back only once the bytes have already landed.",
